{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:15:48.358551Z","id":"86e7d6b474f245c80b0c947e7ba4512adc8cbd6f190a6e9e1ff32b157a64a05b","body":{"detail":"GitContent over DoHost (StubTransport, a Durable Object stub's fetch) and over ArtifactsHost (the ARTIFACTS binding's promises and fetch) finishes only when the Worker's event loop resolves those promises. clax-core's synchronous entry points drive content futures with content::wait (crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs, section Futures), which on wasm32 would spin on a pending promise. The instance Durable Object must reach content only through the Store's async methods. content_store answers worker::Result (a missing REPO binding or an unknown REPO_STORE fails); make one store per Durable Object instance so the Artifacts host's write-token and remote caches are reused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":115},"content_hash":"2dcbb0f1ebe185a4dfe9cd0a52685d35b9a531a556d4e160363fa3a26a693e8e"},"summary":"content_store's stores complete only through the Store's async methods: their futures await JavaScript","tags":["wiring","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:15:48.358648Z","id":"410461b5f84ee3c6e6f5164b8f785d72cf1b887d9e11d80f52a8fcb8f4f24081","body":{"detail":"DoAssets keeps every artifact asset in RepoDO's SQLite storage (the assets table, crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs), the simplest home for the stand-in. With REPO_STORE=artifacts every instance's asset reads and writes still go through that single Durable Object, and an asset over clax-do-vfs's 16 MiB transaction cap cannot be stored. Options: R2 (a binding; wrangler dev --local simulates it), the instance Durable Object's own storage (content_store would take its State), or one RepoDO per instance (content_store would take the instance name).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":115},"content_hash":"2dcbb0f1ebe185a4dfe9cd0a52685d35b9a531a556d4e160363fa3a26a693e8e"},"summary":"Assets live in the one RepoDO (instance 'repos') for every Clax instance, in both REPO_STORE modes","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:15:48.358691Z","id":"4cfd0bde578366cc3d72227b560bb9858ed01782b30ca94f51981899585ab88b","body":{"detail":"RepoDO was chosen, as hosted/src/repo/memory.ts did: content_store needs only env, the Worker serves /git/ by forwarding to RepoDO without the instance Durable Object, and calls cross a boundary as calls to Artifacts do. The cost is one stub fetch per object read, ref read and update.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":198},"end":{"line":268},"content_hash":"39be025dab599fcd99fd658901afdb0b4b6e31b978dd815e222e53ee951377fb"},"summary":"Keep the stand-in's repositories in the instance Durable Object's own storage instead of a separate RepoDO","tags":["revisit:content_store is given the instance's State, or repositories must be isolated per instance","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:15:48.358727Z","id":"338ce969695c0ac88dc36fa3ca0ae2d6c3469ad1a66e2187aa1a910725dcf119","body":{"detail":"As ClaxDb::new (record 03b5bcf0 on crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs): the DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so expect() is the only way to fail. A production object should keep the error and answer every request with it, or open lazily.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":242},"end":{"line":268},"content_hash":"a5dab96d71ea8d470bfd27f8e67f1d67ff0e351e04a19df358db6869084a79c1"},"summary":"RepoDO::new panics when its database cannot be opened, or when REPO_STORE=artifacts and there is no ARTIFACTS binding","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:15:48.358758Z","id":"2180b3a542c9c8090d638c5ac38acdb380d3acea64168e14983e06b5f6eb7f87","body":{"detail":"serve_git applies a push to main per clax-git's rules and answers served.pushed, which RepoDO only logs. GitContent::write_version then refuses every write while main holds a commit that is not a version's (record 5fc9c903 on crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs, which describes the reconcile that lifts it). test-repos.mjs pushes to main last for this reason.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":319},"end":{"line":324},"content_hash":"8a7c6b1e68e0573aa2a0919be6cf15caef256323bb09ed222270408964783519"},"summary":"Pushes to the stand-in are taken but not recorded as versions, so the next publish of the artifact is refused","tags":["depends-on:5fc9c903f53be34fd407d2045e80ecbf2c04bacef81fb971aaf3305f1214448a","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:15:48.358808Z","id":"43eb027ec60badd0bff1b65b46d0ce7193214ac418655c5b132e593089cd697f","body":{"detail":"apply inserts every object of an update in one transaction on clax-do-vfs, whose Limits refuse a transaction past 16 MiB (crates/clax-worker/vfs/src/lib.rs Limits; test-wasm.mjs checks the cap), while ServeOptions::default lets a push carry 64 MiB. delete also drops unheld objects with a scan of git_objects against git_held (db.rs:129) on every repository deletion.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":222},"end":{"line":292},"content_hash":"a1b06d2dcc4746d6cf2f0cd4d0cb38838039916077f74653815b96311ea230a0"},"summary":"The stand-in keeps each git object whole in one row and writes a push or publish in one transaction, so writes over the VFS's 16 MiB transaction cap fail","tags":["limits","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:15:48.358859Z","id":"4170cd9081611f108b9e1f81a59f3e9b4faab8e1453ea603071dbf2dc3b793ff","body":{"detail":"GitContent reads a file through GitVersions::read_file, which reads refs() and walks the tree with read_object; on Artifacts that is a GET of info/refs?service=git-receive-pack plus readTree per directory and readBlob. The binding's readFile({ ref: 'refs/tags/v<n>', path }) answers in one call (ArtifactsRepo::read_file_at), but nothing in the Repo interface reaches it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":375},"end":{"line":383},"content_hash":"0475e7d05b953b9ff565dbf96744595a717c47db40a7c4e1f030fc035fe33f16"},"summary":"Every Artifacts ref read is a receive-pack advertisement over HTTP, so each version file read costs a GET to the remote and a binding call per tree level","tags":["performance","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:15:48.358893Z","id":"24b470e70478dbcb9f99724d4b52777779a046710529cc69ac1139c4b7dcf0b4","body":{"detail":"Tested only over fakes (src/repos/tests/artifacts_fake.rs: clax-git's server in process; artifacts_http_backend.rs: git http-backend). Unverified: (1) the binding call shapes js.rs makes: create(name, { setDefaultBranch }), get, delete, and on a handle info, createToken(scope, ttl), revokeToken(id), fork(name), readCommit, readTree, readBlob, readFile({ ref, path }), Symbol.dispose, and error codes read from e.code; (2) whether readCommit, readTree and readBlob answer null for an object of another type rather than throwing (read_object tries tree, blob, then commit); (3) that a tree rebuilt from readTree's entries hashes back to its ID (mode text, entry order); (4) receive-pack at an Artifacts remote: Bearer acceptance of art_v1_…?expires= tokens, 401 or 403 for an expired one, the atomic and delete-refs capabilities, Clax creating refs/tags/v<n>, and its answer to moving main back; (5) a fork's readiness: a get of the copy right after fork may throw FORK_IN_PROGRESS, which makes GitContent::fork fail and delete the copy; (6) mint and revoke for people through ArtifactsTokens. Under wrangler dev --local the binding's create answered an object without remote (test-repos.mjs prints the message).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"37ebbbb2126f4824c088d7e3c44e3051f5ec86e09bd13bd68dcf39f8603f514b"},"summary":"The Artifacts host has never run against real Cloudflare Artifacts","tags":["untested","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:15:48.358945Z","id":"8dca1da143714a8ce5fd0f0a42251b43e1bcb8c71f624f00ca0c018690b1492f","body":{"detail":"repos::worker::mint_git_token and revoke_git_token are the calls. Exposure, as hosted/src/git/tokens.ts and route.ts did: POST /api/artifacts/{id}/git-token {scope} for a signed-in person, same-origin only, and the MCP git_remote tool for an agent session, both answering the GitToken (remote, token, expires_at, clone_command, jj_clone_command). Rights, in clax-core's Rights::allows: a read token needs the clone right, a write token the push right (the owner, or the owner's agent); an agent's read or write token also needs its person to see every author of the repository's history, else it is withheld (a token cannot filter a clone). Lifetimes PERSON_TOKEN_TTL_S and AGENT_TOKEN_TTL_S; pass the request's public origin. An agent's token must be tracked by its artifact and revoked with revoke_git_token when a version carries work its person may not see, its rights drop or the agent session ends (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts noteGitToken).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":208},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"259557c80b9d285dcbd7eee22bdb7932c4fc7f5cb5b045a73d93621b3f2ae8d1"},"summary":"Nothing serves repository tokens yet: the server's git-token route and MCP git_remote tool should call mint_git_token after their rights checks","tags":["status:deferred","wiring","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:53.813985Z","id":"71f810404fb3a2c0161d91103e37cbd421a14db1082f8b1543f35de5ee90bf2c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"410461b5f84ee3c6e6f5164b8f785d72cf1b887d9e11d80f52a8fcb8f4f24081","summary":"Decided by the owner: assets live in R2 (the ASSETS bucket binding, simulated by wrangler dev --local) in both REPO_STORE modes, not in RepoDO; AssetStore semantics (put/read/delete, unversioned) kept","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:53.814224Z","id":"af3ed5532e106449d9788d748d651d393f1f1827dcd15592d7e2f0df43e7afdd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1edca34f","summary":"Assets are objects in the ASSETS R2 bucket (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/assets.rs BucketAssets over js::R2Objects); RepoDO's assets table and internal asset calls are gone. Evidence: cargo test (repos::tests::assets, 3 tests; the content contract through the internal API with BucketAssets) passes, and node test-repos.mjs prints 'ok   after a restart the asset reads back from R2' and the six 'R2 under REPO_STORE=artifacts' checks","supersedes":"410461b5f84ee3c6e6f5164b8f785d72cf1b887d9e11d80f52a8fcb8f4f24081","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:53.820139Z","id":"a9f6718549faf6ca007829a59a9810f01aa01ca26cd3c61af7681d0cc6ffbc82","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:19967d06","summary":"A write over the VFS cap no longer fails part-way: db::apply refuses objects over MAX_WRITE_BYTES (12 MiB) before its transaction, and RepoDO's serve_options bound a push body and its unpacked size the same. Evidence: cargo test a_write_over_the_bound_is_refused_and_writes_nothing and a_push_over_the_stand_ins_write_bound_is_refused_whole pass; test-repos.mjs prints 'ok   a 13 MiB push is refused 413 and changes nothing' and 'ok   a 10 MiB push fits under the VFS's transaction cap'. The bound itself and the delete scan are recorded anew on db.rs","supersedes":"43eb027ec60badd0bff1b65b46d0ce7193214ac418655c5b132e593089cd697f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:53.826295Z","id":"49db54dc96a10adae827fae9d2e561e5eb9f0a4cbd5b9f8d7285b88e1a43afc6","body":{"detail":"MAX_WRITE_BYTES keeps a write under clax-do-vfs's 16 MiB transaction cap (vfs/src/lib.rs MAX_TRANSACTION_BYTES) with room for rows and indexes: a version or push carrying more is refused, invalid_argument, with the bound in the message (git shows it after 'remote:' or as HTTP 413). Each object is one row, whole, so a single file over the bound can never be stored. Artifacts allows 32 MB per blob and 1 GB per repository. delete (db.rs:117) runs DELETE FROM git_objects WHERE id NOT IN (SELECT id FROM git_held), a scan of every object, on each repository deletion.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":48},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"6183d1a70eeca3ee16eaaf4607a156c177d6eb02f1ae847cba00067497ce28a4"},"summary":"The stand-in takes at most 12 MiB of objects in one push or publish, and drops unheld objects with a full scan on every repository deletion","tags":["limits","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:53.826426Z","id":"975cd323d9648e2f2d0b00a90c976b88d109d26aa1a6710cb9162d7cb3d5efb8","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"24b470e70478dbcb9f99724d4b52777779a046710529cc69ac1139c4b7dcf0b4","summary":"Point (5) is handled per Cloudflare's docs (developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/api/workers-binding: get 'throws if the repo ... is not ready yet'; api/errors: FORK_IN_PROGRESS 10303, IMPORT_IN_PROGRESS 10302): get_ready (artifacts.rs) retries after each of READY_WAITS_MS and a fork waits for its copy (commit f9bc642f, tests a_fork_waits_while_artifacts_is_still_making_the_copy and a_fork_still_in_progress_after_the_bounded_wait_deletes_its_copy_and_a_retry_succeeds). Still unverified against the service: that the thrown error carries e.code as that string, and whether a token of a deleted repository works on a repository later created under the same name (the docs say tokens are repo-scoped; ArtifactsHost::delete does not mark the ledger's rows revoked)","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:53.826780Z","id":"920522a35e742125dc495dfcb3c03a4d7c363286328c854e5a6239c82b18a7de","body":{"detail":"tokens::mint asks the host for the token, then its remote, then writes the ledger row. On Cloudflare Artifacts createToken has made a live token by then; if remote() (a get and info()) or insert_token fails, mint answers the error and the token is neither returned nor in git_tokens, so nothing can revoke it before its TTL (at most what the caller asked, PERSON_TOKEN_TTL_S or AGENT_TOKEN_TTL_S). Ask for the remote first, or enter the row in the must-revoke list when the insert fails.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":222},"end":{"line":231},"content_hash":"c667618df305315f9bf6e87e95ecf9d1b1d0d11e97765683683367609cef2976"},"summary":"A token the host minted is live but untracked when remote() or the ledger insert fails after it","tags":["security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:53.827012Z","id":"f059410508242a9b8c7e4abb2304b244687fcb5ada215c7b1e636d15758f5f8f","body":{"detail":"RepoDO::new runs repo_store(&env).unwrap_or(RepoStore::Memory), so with a mistyped REPO_STORE it mints stand-in tokens and keeps a stand-in ledger, while content_store fails 'Unknown REPO_STORE' and git_http_serving answers false. Nothing is exposed (no stand-in repository is created), but the misconfiguration surfaces only on content calls; RepoDO should answer every request with the error, as record 338ce969 suggests for its other construction failures.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":291},"end":{"line":291},"content_hash":"12759c7368cc3bb5d16b885acab3a48cc5b57cca42c60447d4ff7ea5ffb8a13d"},"summary":"RepoDO takes an unknown REPO_STORE for memory while content_store and forward_git refuse it","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:39:25.895253Z","id":"ada1dc0a690272e30e2dd988f06571c8eb31911de3c4f57e9c7ad5f03ec6de44","body":{"detail":"GitContent over DoHost (StubTransport, a Durable Object stub's fetch) and over ArtifactsHost (the ARTIFACTS binding's promises and fetch) finishes only when the Worker's event loop resolves those promises. clax-core's synchronous entry points drive content futures with content::wait (crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs, section Futures), which on wasm32 would spin on a pending promise. The instance Durable Object must reach content only through the Store's async methods. content_store answers worker::Result (a missing REPO binding or an unknown REPO_STORE fails); make one store per Durable Object instance so the Artifacts host's write-token and remote caches are reused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"89e4b1f15cd6c1509dd4d9f749e6b11a5068f31e4c051f4443d1734166d323df"},"summary":"content_store's stores complete only through the Store's async methods: their futures await JavaScript","supersedes":"86e7d6b474f245c80b0c947e7ba4512adc8cbd6f190a6e9e1ff32b157a64a05b","tags":["wiring","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:39:25.901389Z","id":"3f0df37e429e49e961d8ecdce1b384ff8cb7a043d49d89e7bebf2fa3716f2065","body":{"detail":"RepoDO was chosen, as hosted/src/repo/memory.ts did: content_store needs only env, the Worker serves /git/ by forwarding to RepoDO without the instance Durable Object, and calls cross a boundary as calls to Artifacts do. The cost is one stub fetch per object read, ref read and update.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":213},"end":{"line":311},"content_hash":"e80acc5d489323262469e3beae7e559b843216715c932a7c40f50a1e4fc282ea"},"summary":"Keep the stand-in's repositories in the instance Durable Object's own storage instead of a separate RepoDO","supersedes":"4cfd0bde578366cc3d72227b560bb9858ed01782b30ca94f51981899585ab88b","tags":["revisit:content_store is given the instance's State, or repositories must be isolated per instance","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:39:25.907531Z","id":"f214afdc252e1382a430b37a6d4e2e63541e172b2dc6514a11b617d672304180","body":{"detail":"As ClaxDb::new (record 03b5bcf0 on crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs): the DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so expect() is the only way to fail. A production object should keep the error and answer every request with it, or open lazily.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":285},"end":{"line":311},"content_hash":"39e2fa95f14c80a5ef8617ce841897dd597cad541dbe2c89efa62f384c256ab3"},"summary":"RepoDO::new panics when its database cannot be opened, or when REPO_STORE=artifacts and there is no ARTIFACTS binding","supersedes":"338ce969695c0ac88dc36fa3ca0ae2d6c3469ad1a66e2187aa1a910725dcf119","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:39:25.910275Z","id":"f123b0cf25e174e3022cdf26a8c315f8e898dada536516b4945f182ed20a2a3a","body":{"detail":"serve_git applies a push to main per clax-git's rules and answers served.pushed, which RepoDO only logs. GitContent::write_version then refuses every write while main holds a commit that is not a version's (record 5fc9c903 on crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs, which describes the reconcile that lifts it). test-repos.mjs pushes to main last for this reason.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":368},"end":{"line":373},"content_hash":"8a7c6b1e68e0573aa2a0919be6cf15caef256323bb09ed222270408964783519"},"summary":"Pushes to the stand-in are taken but not recorded as versions, so the next publish of the artifact is refused","supersedes":"2180b3a542c9c8090d638c5ac38acdb380d3acea64168e14983e06b5f6eb7f87","tags":["depends-on:5fc9c903f53be34fd407d2045e80ecbf2c04bacef81fb971aaf3305f1214448a","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:39:25.912387Z","id":"ae1683edc7facfa5dba595d726b061aab3f6fdb03da2490394427f5a48d02d17","body":{"detail":"GitContent reads a file through GitVersions::read_file, which reads refs() and walks the tree with read_object; on Artifacts that is a GET of info/refs?service=git-receive-pack plus readTree per directory and readBlob. The binding's readFile({ ref: 'refs/tags/v<n>', path }) answers in one call (ArtifactsRepo::read_file_at), but nothing in the Repo interface reaches it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":423},"end":{"line":431},"content_hash":"0475e7d05b953b9ff565dbf96744595a717c47db40a7c4e1f030fc035fe33f16"},"summary":"Every Artifacts ref read is a receive-pack advertisement over HTTP, so each version file read costs a GET to the remote and a binding call per tree level","supersedes":"4170cd9081611f108b9e1f81a59f3e9b4faab8e1453ea603071dbf2dc3b793ff","tags":["performance","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:39:25.914459Z","id":"926398ef37f0bbe8b8c2bf022ac5065c916dc3fe2a17426727e30cc45163fdc0","body":{"detail":"Tested only over fakes (src/repos/tests/artifacts_fake.rs: clax-git's server in process; artifacts_http_backend.rs: git http-backend). Unverified: (1) the binding call shapes js.rs makes: create(name, { setDefaultBranch }), get, delete, and on a handle info, createToken(scope, ttl), revokeToken(id), fork(name), readCommit, readTree, readBlob, readFile({ ref, path }), Symbol.dispose, and error codes read from e.code; (2) whether readCommit, readTree and readBlob answer null for an object of another type rather than throwing (read_object tries tree, blob, then commit); (3) that a tree rebuilt from readTree's entries hashes back to its ID (mode text, entry order); (4) receive-pack at an Artifacts remote: Bearer acceptance of art_v1_…?expires= tokens, 401 or 403 for an expired one, the atomic and delete-refs capabilities, Clax creating refs/tags/v<n>, and its answer to moving main back; (5) a fork's readiness: a get of the copy right after fork may throw FORK_IN_PROGRESS, which makes GitContent::fork fail and delete the copy; (6) mint and revoke for people through ArtifactsTokens. Under wrangler dev --local the binding's create answered an object without remote (test-repos.mjs prints the message).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":72},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"9a584f6c061033bffa204a7bb6168acdf514f76ade4e6355107734a878ebb9e4"},"summary":"The Artifacts host has never run against real Cloudflare Artifacts","supersedes":"24b470e70478dbcb9f99724d4b52777779a046710529cc69ac1139c4b7dcf0b4","tags":["untested","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:17:17.927272Z","id":"94d8be2f4a4293d966b5a4dfa9d13590ea8e36c1f3f87b28de8e8beb41809c9c","body":{"detail":"RepoDO::new runs repo_store(&env).unwrap_or(RepoStore::Memory), so with a mistyped REPO_STORE it mints stand-in tokens and keeps a stand-in ledger, while content_store fails 'Unknown REPO_STORE' and git_http_serving answers false. Nothing is exposed (no stand-in repository is created), but the misconfiguration surfaces only on content calls; RepoDO should answer every request with the error, as record 338ce969 suggests for its other construction failures.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":304},"end":{"line":304},"content_hash":"12759c7368cc3bb5d16b885acab3a48cc5b57cca42c60447d4ff7ea5ffb8a13d"},"summary":"RepoDO takes an unknown REPO_STORE for memory while content_store and forward_git refuse it","supersedes":"f059410508242a9b8c7e4abb2304b244687fcb5ada215c7b1e636d15758f5f8f","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:17:17.929404Z","id":"28185a5e5c57c96ede77a9992237106b2e9e4244e4c50f0156e2d4090e142ab7","body":{"detail":"RepoDO was chosen, as hosted/src/repo/memory.ts did: content_store needs only env, the Worker serves /git/ by forwarding to RepoDO without the instance Durable Object, and calls cross a boundary as calls to Artifacts do. The cost is one stub fetch per object read, ref read and update.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":239},"end":{"line":324},"content_hash":"fac5e0e32b5265d0b1b6ff39c5c45cc4fe413ef5831b038a115f37092b962d64"},"summary":"Keep the stand-in's repositories in the instance Durable Object's own storage instead of a separate RepoDO","supersedes":"3f0df37e429e49e961d8ecdce1b384ff8cb7a043d49d89e7bebf2fa3716f2065","tags":["revisit:content_store is given the instance's State, or repositories must be isolated per instance","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:17:17.931540Z","id":"7bb13b9516a8b10919bbac9f3e6bc9f36d628e6852b391ffc257d6438a9480b5","body":{"detail":"As ClaxDb::new (record 03b5bcf0 on crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs): the DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so expect() is the only way to fail. A production object should keep the error and answer every request with it, or open lazily.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":298},"end":{"line":324},"content_hash":"39e2fa95f14c80a5ef8617ce841897dd597cad541dbe2c89efa62f384c256ab3"},"summary":"RepoDO::new panics when its database cannot be opened, or when REPO_STORE=artifacts and there is no ARTIFACTS binding","supersedes":"f214afdc252e1382a430b37a6d4e2e63541e172b2dc6514a11b617d672304180","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:17:17.933656Z","id":"1b9d70faeac151281e55452750d0d58b2df251b08114176c70a4ad2fcc1f874b","body":{"detail":"serve_git applies a push to main per clax-git's rules and answers served.pushed, which RepoDO only logs. GitContent::write_version then refuses every write while main holds a commit that is not a version's (record 5fc9c903 on crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs, which describes the reconcile that lifts it). test-repos.mjs pushes to main last for this reason.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":381},"end":{"line":386},"content_hash":"8a7c6b1e68e0573aa2a0919be6cf15caef256323bb09ed222270408964783519"},"summary":"Pushes to the stand-in are taken but not recorded as versions, so the next publish of the artifact is refused","supersedes":"f123b0cf25e174e3022cdf26a8c315f8e898dada536516b4945f182ed20a2a3a","tags":["depends-on:5fc9c903f53be34fd407d2045e80ecbf2c04bacef81fb971aaf3305f1214448a","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:38:24.041208Z","id":"be44cf3c7cc7456bb81e587fe1de09074823753e84fc9c4f484c261753aac42b","body":{"detail":"ArtifactsHost::can_prune is false because Artifacts has no call that drops a repository's objects, and an Artifacts fork would keep every object the source held, including versions after the forked one, for its git server to hand to a want naming them. So clax_git::versions::fork_at reads every commit, tree and file the forked version reaches from the source (ArtifactsRepo::read_object, one blob/tree/commit binding call each, crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs read_object) and pushes them to a new repository in one receive-pack request. A fork of a long or large history costs that many calls and one pack of its whole size. Never measured against real Artifacts (record 926398ef). Options: a server-side Artifacts call that forks at a commit, if Artifacts gains one; or reading the history as one upload-pack fetch from the source.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":491},"end":{"line":506},"content_hash":"2b58712df9f07c0ca9e51ac3fa2868da781b62c15c0f878098256a494fd81638"},"summary":"On Artifacts a fork is a new repository written with every object the forked version reaches, read one binding call at a time, not an Artifacts fork","tags":["perf","revisit:Artifacts offers a fork at a commit, or a fork is measured slow","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:00:41.053786Z","id":"753c9240d895c9f1b42f9f08d1d3ca786e78e7bc989a9a7be18655b651bde957","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8dca1da143714a8ce5fd0f0a42251b43e1bcb8c71f624f00ca0c018690b1492f","summary":"Since c3df54b3 mint_git_token takes the token's Holder (person public ID, none for the owner; agent session ID): the git-token route must pass the signed-in person and the MCP git_remote tool the agent's person and session, or every push with their tokens is recorded as the owner's (RepoDO::record_push, crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs:317:346).","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:01:12.031328Z","id":"88b10d4553b0ed7be913fdfe5c23064ef38017b76964e0e5ce494f462ded41fb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c3df54b3","summary":"RepoDO records a push to the stand-in as versions before answering it (RepoDO::record_push → the instance's /_internal/pushed). node test-repos.mjs (CLAX_TEST_JJ set): 53 checks ok, among them 'a git push to main is version 2 once the push is answered', 'a jj git push to main is version 3, carrying version 2's other files', 'a publish that did not see the pushes conflicts', 'a publish after the pushes lands as version 4'.","supersedes":"1b9d70faeac151281e55452750d0d58b2df251b08114176c70a4ad2fcc1f874b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.354459Z","id":"5aaa4d81eeb6f3d689fa1dac9f27328090191b0eca61c8990121ea5ec1f4abd2","body":{"detail":"MAX_WRITE_BYTES keeps a write under clax-do-vfs's 16 MiB transaction cap (vfs/src/lib.rs MAX_TRANSACTION_BYTES) with room for rows and indexes: a version or push carrying more is refused, invalid_argument, with the bound in the message (git shows it after 'remote:' or as HTTP 413). Each object is one row, whole, so a single file over the bound can never be stored. Artifacts allows 32 MB per blob and 1 GB per repository. delete (db.rs:117) runs DELETE FROM git_objects WHERE id NOT IN (SELECT id FROM git_held), a scan of every object, on each repository deletion.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"6183d1a70eeca3ee16eaaf4607a156c177d6eb02f1ae847cba00067497ce28a4"},"summary":"The stand-in takes at most 12 MiB of objects in one push or publish, and drops unheld objects with a full scan on every repository deletion","supersedes":"49db54dc96a10adae827fae9d2e561e5eb9f0a4cbd5b9f8d7285b88e1a43afc6","tags":["limits","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.385358Z","id":"99e223550f84959cf44ccde359dd5b339568547a9074ba82b388ab0888f58e1e","body":{"detail":"repos::worker::mint_git_token and revoke_git_token are the calls. Exposure, as hosted/src/git/tokens.ts and route.ts did: POST /api/artifacts/{id}/git-token {scope} for a signed-in person, same-origin only, and the MCP git_remote tool for an agent session, both answering the GitToken (remote, token, expires_at, clone_command, jj_clone_command). Rights, in clax-core's Rights::allows: a read token needs the clone right, a write token the push right (the owner, or the owner's agent); an agent's read or write token also needs its person to see every author of the repository's history, else it is withheld (a token cannot filter a clone). Lifetimes PERSON_TOKEN_TTL_S and AGENT_TOKEN_TTL_S; pass the request's public origin. An agent's token must be tracked by its artifact and revoked with revoke_git_token when a version carries work its person may not see, its rights drop or the agent session ends (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts noteGitToken).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":220},"end":{"line":254},"content_hash":"6514439517b5038e56a3f358a0b6206ecb890bdf8d145c7ca4c01e6692f0ca71"},"summary":"Nothing serves repository tokens yet: the server's git-token route and MCP git_remote tool should call mint_git_token after their rights checks","supersedes":"8dca1da143714a8ce5fd0f0a42251b43e1bcb8c71f624f00ca0c018690b1492f","tags":["status:deferred","wiring","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.389586Z","id":"8e60c81a2218e10787dc9044745317712e2afd4563c40833b4194b0b5e16f92e","body":{"detail":"tokens::mint asks the host for the token, then its remote, then writes the ledger row. On Cloudflare Artifacts createToken has made a live token by then; if remote() (a get and info()) or insert_token fails, mint answers the error and the token is neither returned nor in git_tokens, so nothing can revoke it before its TTL (at most what the caller asked, PERSON_TOKEN_TTL_S or AGENT_TOKEN_TTL_S). Ask for the remote first, or enter the row in the must-revoke list when the insert fails.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":235},"end":{"line":245},"content_hash":"b8ece7fef497593a251599cd340472d0c2db6aa91ef14618db26be51da22c4c7"},"summary":"A token the host minted is live but untracked when remote() or the ledger insert fails after it","supersedes":"920522a35e742125dc495dfcb3c03a4d7c363286328c854e5a6239c82b18a7de","tags":["security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.393725Z","id":"11f3b0bc6fe0b23ee6d393c763b8c3e99a6b6eddee44086743d008934b71b8a2","body":{"detail":"Rights are rechecked only when a pushed commit is recorded (crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs Store::standing), and agents' tokens are revoked only when a new version or a refused commit carries an author their person may not see (revoke_blind_tokens). Nothing revokes a holder's repository tokens on Store::revoke_person, set_person_rights or a narrowing that drops clone or push, grant revoke, or session end, so they keep cloning (and a write token pushing, its commits then refused) for up to PERSON_TOKEN_TTL_S or AGENT_TOKEN_TTL_S. Between a push landing and its reconcile, an agent's token whose person may not see the pusher can also fetch the pushed commit. The hosted prototype revokes on rights changes and agent end (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts revokeForRights, agentEnded). Revocations are logged with tracing only; no audit kind records them. Fix: on those changes, revoke the holder's tokens of every repository through ContentStore::repo_tokens and revoke_repo_token (a listener as people.rs's others are).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":220},"end":{"line":254},"content_hash":"6514439517b5038e56a3f358a0b6206ecb890bdf8d145c7ca4c01e6692f0ca71"},"summary":"A revoked or narrowed person's, or an ended agent's, repository tokens keep fetching and pushing until they expire","tags":["security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.140172Z","id":"7cb29ff19968d57557e53418ddc6824c20670d18c0a79bab3a02e1b2524f82d8","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"11f3b0bc6fe0b23ee6d393c763b8c3e99a6b6eddee44086743d008934b71b8a2","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.140257Z","id":"3661db1075a43e3f52b7454832adfbf1654df0f59d177b006a2ef242896c4772","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"99e223550f84959cf44ccde359dd5b339568547a9074ba82b388ab0888f58e1e","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.140343Z","id":"66080dfad2a25e975cb4b9cabae2e9c63f1ead4cb0ddd8f4e5f0bc3bf532d81a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"28185a5e5c57c96ede77a9992237106b2e9e4244e4c50f0156e2d4090e142ab7","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:25:53.949491Z","id":"811546f8c085d3e8ad086d3e9dd81fcf4b8c6e65e1db2c2f9432c5915536be41","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1b285a7b","summary":"Fixed: POST /api/artifacts/{aid}/git-token (people, same origin) and POST /api/sessions/{id}/git-token/{aid} (agent sessions, the MCP git_remote tool) mint through clax_server::git_remotes::GitRemotes, which the Worker implements over RepoDO (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/remotes.rs), after Rights::allows (read for clone, update for push) and, for agents, the history visibility check; tokens carry their Holder. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_git_tokens passes 9/9; clax-worker repos::tests::remotes passes (a person's write token pushes a version credited to her); node test-repos.mjs passes its route checks under wrangler dev.","supersedes":"99e223550f84959cf44ccde359dd5b339568547a9074ba82b388ab0888f58e1e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:25:53.953754Z","id":"6ef24c074038a27384d950efd40d3fc4be460153a8f39f9044d56ec096a92294","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0a6d46ae","summary":"Fixed: ending a session by any path that stops it (feedback::sessions_stop) revokes its tokens by holder; narrowing a person's rights or revoking them revokes theirs and their agents' before the route answers; narrowing a grant revokes its live sessions'. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_git_tokens passes 9/9, including an_agents_token_is_revoked_when_its_session_ends, a_persons_tokens_are_revoked_when_their_rights_narrow_or_they_are_revoked and the grant narrowing in an_agent_whose_person_may_not_see_an_author_...; test-repos.mjs 'an ended session's token clones nothing' passes on the Worker.","supersedes":"11f3b0bc6fe0b23ee6d393c763b8c3e99a6b6eddee44086743d008934b71b8a2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.093613Z","id":"b9f925d3835b657d6d6bd5a6e84de3e2a1c193a9798ab0ab0b4af5c38a013c25","body":{"detail":"GitContent over DoHost (StubTransport, a Durable Object stub's fetch) and over ArtifactsHost (the ARTIFACTS binding's promises and fetch) finishes only when the Worker's event loop resolves those promises. clax-core's synchronous entry points drive content futures with content::wait (crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs, section Futures), which on wasm32 would spin on a pending promise. The instance Durable Object must reach content only through the Store's async methods. content_store answers worker::Result (a missing REPO binding or an unknown REPO_STORE fails); make one store per Durable Object instance so the Artifacts host's write-token and remote caches are reused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":111},"end":{"line":133},"content_hash":"ee9e7329be97a8181d5f4b5b7975b72d91cf1fc204b6d18f1a41257156fa4d09"},"summary":"content_store's stores complete only through the Store's async methods: their futures await JavaScript","supersedes":"ada1dc0a690272e30e2dd988f06571c8eb31911de3c4f57e9c7ad5f03ec6de44","tags":["wiring","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.098020Z","id":"65cd3397fd2fea8329eaac0479674bf527f31728f8cacd1ab9ff1bc45b4913a9","body":{"detail":"RepoDO was chosen, as hosted/src/repo/memory.ts did: content_store needs only env, the Worker serves /git/ by forwarding to RepoDO without the instance Durable Object, and calls cross a boundary as calls to Artifacts do. The cost is one stub fetch per object read, ref read and update.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":252},"end":{"line":337},"content_hash":"de910bc71178dda8e13b591e6306afbb6eb2ff1ea69f7e4edcac1d48bab17331"},"summary":"Keep the stand-in's repositories in the instance Durable Object's own storage instead of a separate RepoDO","supersedes":"28185a5e5c57c96ede77a9992237106b2e9e4244e4c50f0156e2d4090e142ab7","tags":["revisit:content_store is given the instance's State, or repositories must be isolated per instance","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.102459Z","id":"f042bcc9287d3292d81016d91828a06a0616bd24ac70035ffcc9c6ff7dbe0e5f","body":{"detail":"As ClaxDb::new (record 03b5bcf0 on crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs): the DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so expect() is the only way to fail. A production object should keep the error and answer every request with it, or open lazily.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":311},"end":{"line":337},"content_hash":"41e82060ef2ed7a3d37c731ee3f07aea84963861504255cae5ac7b030496ccb1"},"summary":"RepoDO::new panics when its database cannot be opened, or when REPO_STORE=artifacts and there is no ARTIFACTS binding","supersedes":"7bb13b9516a8b10919bbac9f3e6bc9f36d628e6852b391ffc257d6438a9480b5","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.106853Z","id":"85d4a7a24ea5c6ebf01333c98cd4b66c3589e1e739fb8e0e78af70d6ea01d226","body":{"detail":"RepoDO::new runs repo_store(&env).unwrap_or(RepoStore::Memory), so with a mistyped REPO_STORE it mints stand-in tokens and keeps a stand-in ledger, while content_store fails 'Unknown REPO_STORE' and git_http_serving answers false. Nothing is exposed (no stand-in repository is created), but the misconfiguration surfaces only on content calls; RepoDO should answer every request with the error, as record 338ce969 suggests for its other construction failures.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":317},"end":{"line":317},"content_hash":"10ae4d6536445b45ee3d2b247be03ba480325bc30df54317405eda43ad3df29f"},"summary":"RepoDO takes an unknown REPO_STORE for memory while content_store and forward_git refuse it","supersedes":"94d8be2f4a4293d966b5a4dfa9d13590ea8e36c1f3f87b28de8e8beb41809c9c","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/git_http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372059Z","id":"1f2c4ec03414c1b286d3112a67bf7c6f5a64bbe6bc18978b3470416082f34678","body":{"detail":"serve_git answers upload-pack for any live token of the repository (tokens::check). After a push RepoDO awaits crate::reconcile_pushes (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs record_push), and revoke_blind_tokens runs only inside that reconcile, so an agent session's read token whose person may not see the pusher can `git fetch` main at the pushed commit in that window and read the pusher's words unfiltered. git_remotes::mint_for refuses a mint while unrecorded pushes exist (check_history, 503 repo_unavailable), but serving a fetch has no matching check. A rule like 'refuse upload-pack to a session-held token while main is past the newest v<n> tag' would also refuse it while main ends in refused commits, which stay on main until someone pushes over them, so the check needs the instance's view of which commits are refused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"4637647a8d5a05cb35a10683a995eb897d960be4f26ec20367022730f67dd319"},"suggested_fix":"Have RepoDO hold a per-repository 'recording' flag across the reconcile await and answer 503 repo_unavailable to upload-pack from a session-held token while it is set, or advertise main at the newest recorded commit to such tokens.","summary":"An agent's read token fetches a teammate's pushed commit before the instance records it and revokes the token","tags":["security","visibility","worker","git","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372401Z","id":"3a0b3f5e612d0e20bc09478077ddadae7533faf06a94197a7d92b1b43b30e1ba","body":{"detail":"RepoDO::new calls expect on DoPageStore::new, clax_do_vfs::open, LocalHost::new and artifacts_binding. A panic on wasm32 aborts the whole isolate, every Durable Object in it included (the instance object too), and the next request builds RepoDO again and panics again while the cause lasts. InstanceDo keeps its build error and answers 500 instead (and builds again at the next event).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":360},"end":{"line":376},"content_hash":"bee584e6fcf535f7d2423571924ff3b63b2f8255baeb46d6b6f702bd17d25530"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the error in RepoDO (as InstanceDo::inner does), answer 503 from fetch, and build again at the next request.","summary":"RepoDO's constructor panics on a storage error or a missing ARTIFACTS binding, which aborts the isolate","tags":["worker","panic","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:46.896807Z","id":"1f283ade28fd3338a6edca030832b16f1086dee4267b8a8f4384851f95af8a16","body":{"detail":"RepoDO was chosen, as hosted/src/repo/memory.ts did: content_store needs only env, the Worker serves /git/ by forwarding to RepoDO without the instance Durable Object, and calls cross a boundary as calls to Artifacts do. The cost is one stub fetch per object read, ref read and update.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":255},"end":{"line":340},"content_hash":"de910bc71178dda8e13b591e6306afbb6eb2ff1ea69f7e4edcac1d48bab17331"},"summary":"Keep the stand-in's repositories in the instance Durable Object's own storage instead of a separate RepoDO","supersedes":"65cd3397fd2fea8329eaac0479674bf527f31728f8cacd1ab9ff1bc45b4913a9","tags":["revisit:content_store is given the instance's State, or repositories must be isolated per instance","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:46.902931Z","id":"a8df47c875e190a12525e8ac933ca54d40d72d61783ec6e960121f25f0b7e45e","body":{"detail":"As ClaxDb::new (record 03b5bcf0 on crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs): the DurableObject constructor is synchronous and returns Self, so expect() is the only way to fail. A production object should keep the error and answer every request with it, or open lazily.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":314},"end":{"line":340},"content_hash":"41e82060ef2ed7a3d37c731ee3f07aea84963861504255cae5ac7b030496ccb1"},"summary":"RepoDO::new panics when its database cannot be opened, or when REPO_STORE=artifacts and there is no ARTIFACTS binding","supersedes":"f042bcc9287d3292d81016d91828a06a0616bd24ac70035ffcc9c6ff7dbe0e5f","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:46.909048Z","id":"ca3c96c535ecb30457946bf97b16485f3532260c2fc452702f650022ae197e87","body":{"detail":"RepoDO::new runs repo_store(&env).unwrap_or(RepoStore::Memory), so with a mistyped REPO_STORE it mints stand-in tokens and keeps a stand-in ledger, while content_store fails 'Unknown REPO_STORE' and git_http_serving answers false. Nothing is exposed (no stand-in repository is created), but the misconfiguration surfaces only on content calls; RepoDO should answer every request with the error, as record 338ce969 suggests for its other construction failures.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":320},"end":{"line":320},"content_hash":"10ae4d6536445b45ee3d2b247be03ba480325bc30df54317405eda43ad3df29f"},"summary":"RepoDO takes an unknown REPO_STORE for memory while content_store and forward_git refuse it","supersedes":"85d4a7a24ea5c6ebf01333c98cd4b66c3589e1e739fb8e0e78af70d6ea01d226","tags":["error-handling","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:55.785204Z","id":"e1d187f2470e4f8c3e90129b9b8bae2e16c921945af7618cd1b2304359eb7d60","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a8df47c875e190a12525e8ac933ca54d40d72d61783ec6e960121f25f0b7e45e","summary":"RepoDO::new's expect calls are at crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs:360:376 (DoPageStore::new, clax_do_vfs::open, LocalHost::new, artifacts_binding). A panic there on wasm32 aborts the isolate, the instance object with it, and the next request builds RepoDO again and panics again while the cause lasts; InstanceDo now keeps its build error and builds again at the next event (6838f1bf), which RepoDO could follow.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:20:08.300600Z","id":"45678d5996c039495c0304fd5a4ec6b9d67cea0ce930691b823ee856cdc01b40","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of a8df47c875e190a12525e8ac933ca54d40d72d61783ec6e960121f25f0b7e45e (RepoDO::new panics), on the same constructor; the isolate-abort point is a reply there","supersedes":"3a0b3f5e612d0e20bc09478077ddadae7533faf06a94197a7d92b1b43b30e1ba","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:34:23.231043Z","id":"a2f9296e25831105e1a460340f3d56dc0a439a3a3c9f4dc3cbc2d12fab65b317","body":{"detail":"Found under wrangler dev --local with REPO_STORE=memory and node smoke-remote.mjs --local --probe: the binding answered every call with an RpcPromise (not instanceof Promise), and once awaited each threw 'The RPC receiver does not implement the method \"apply\"'. Since 5f137623 crates/clax-worker/src/repos/js.rs call() uses Reflect.apply and Promise.resolve, and the same probe gets 'Binding ARTIFACTS needs to be run remotely', the local binding's real refusal. The binding's documented shapes (@cloudflare/workers-types 5.20261014.1: createToken -> {id, plaintext, scope, expiresAt}; readCommit -> {hash, treeHash, message, author{name,email}, committer, parents, authoredAt, committedAt} or null; readTree -> [{name, mode, hash, type}] or null; readFile({ref, path}) -> Blob or null; get throws NOT_FOUND / IMPORT_IN_PROGRESS / FORK_IN_PROGRESS) match what js.rs reads. Still unverified on the service; crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs's probe step (src/diag.rs) checks each against a deployed Worker and names any difference.","kind":"comment","references":"926398ef37f0bbe8b8c2bf022ac5065c916dc3fe2a17426727e30cc45163fdc0","summary":"Before 5f137623 no call on the real binding could have worked: js.rs called stub methods with Function.prototype.apply (a remote call named apply on an RPC stub) and returned RpcPromises unawaited","tags":["artifacts","deploy","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:34:23.231359Z","id":"5208791c39a3c76dd1a4fb25e2410b056e6676d52556bd2af8ecba386b198f2d","body":{"detail":"@cloudflare/workers-types 5.20261014.1 lists ArtifactsErrorCode CREATE_IN_PROGRESS beside IMPORT_IN_PROGRESS and FORK_IN_PROGRESS; workerd 1.20260925.1's types (the pinned wrangler's) do not. If the service answers it for a get right after create, publishing a new artifact's first version would fail instead of waiting. smoke-remote.mjs's probe prints what get(repo) answers right after create.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":129},"end":{"line":151},"content_hash":"da65439dd0fa4e0345e0ecb1f83806c0f5753bbb43d862bf7da0fd9d2d116a09"},"suggested_fix":"Treat CREATE_IN_PROGRESS as in_progress (RepoUnavailable prefixed with the code) so get_ready waits for it.","summary":"error_for_code and in_progress do not know CREATE_IN_PROGRESS, which the binding's current types list: a get() of a repository still being created is a plain RepoUnavailable, not retried by get_ready","tags":["artifacts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:34:23.231533Z","id":"0bd1bb641b43d8763e760e60f0000a191bfd9e071c7afe164a9f526a1d158064","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"99e223550f84959cf44ccde359dd5b339568547a9074ba82b388ab0888f58e1e","summary":"Since ef1150ee POST /_diag/repos/token (crates/clax-worker/src/diag.rs, CLAX_DIAG_ROUTES=1 and the owner token) mints an owner-held token for smoke-remote.mjs's git steps; it is not the server's route, which still does not exist","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:04:35.029132Z","id":"597892f4a083d5f12dcfaf64b36802d7bb836ab62dc3952fc15c0f9ec2635a5f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:27a48a40","summary":"error_for_code and in_progress take CREATE_IN_PROGRESS like FORK_IN_PROGRESS, so get_ready waits for a repository still being created. Evidence: crates/clax-worker cargo test artifacts_fake: 13 passed, among them a_first_version_waits_while_artifacts_is_still_creating_the_repository and a_repository_still_being_created_after_the_bounded_wait_is_unavailable (fake binding answering CREATE_IN_PROGRESS).","supersedes":"5208791c39a3c76dd1a4fb25e2410b056e6676d52556bd2af8ecba386b198f2d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"9cf459934b0a2e526c468f80146c08ce0bd729f77021529ca80d022b67b37a46","body":{"detail":"GitContent reads a file through GitVersions::read_file, which reads refs() and walks the tree with read_object; on Artifacts that is a GET of info/refs?service=git-receive-pack plus readTree per directory and readBlob. The binding's readFile({ ref: 'refs/tags/v<n>', path }) answers in one call (ArtifactsRepo::read_file_at), but nothing in the Repo interface reaches it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":426},"end":{"line":434},"content_hash":"0475e7d05b953b9ff565dbf96744595a717c47db40a7c4e1f030fc035fe33f16"},"summary":"Every Artifacts ref read is a receive-pack advertisement over HTTP, so each version file read costs a GET to the remote and a binding call per tree level","supersedes":"ae1683edc7facfa5dba595d726b061aab3f6fdb03da2490394427f5a48d02d17","tags":["performance","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"50b1d2c44c558739377cf97195f75c29351940e5fa5c531182ec21eda0105928","body":{"detail":"ArtifactsHost::can_prune is false because Artifacts has no call that drops a repository's objects, and an Artifacts fork would keep every object the source held, including versions after the forked one, for its git server to hand to a want naming them. So clax_git::versions::fork_at reads every commit, tree and file the forked version reaches from the source (ArtifactsRepo::read_object, one blob/tree/commit binding call each, crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs read_object) and pushes them to a new repository in one receive-pack request. A fork of a long or large history costs that many calls and one pack of its whole size. Never measured against real Artifacts (record 926398ef). Options: a server-side Artifacts call that forks at a commit, if Artifacts gains one; or reading the history as one upload-pack fetch from the source.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":494},"end":{"line":509},"content_hash":"2b58712df9f07c0ca9e51ac3fa2868da781b62c15c0f878098256a494fd81638"},"summary":"On Artifacts a fork is a new repository written with every object the forked version reaches, read one binding call at a time, not an Artifacts fork","supersedes":"be44cf3c7cc7456bb81e587fe1de09074823753e84fc9c4f484c261753aac42b","tags":["perf","revisit:Artifacts offers a fork at a commit, or a fork is measured slow","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"33f6301cd21b287c549f987f0b0a3b0298a8ef68e7da0b21dbbee0721fabd1ff","body":{"detail":"MAX_WRITE_BYTES keeps a write under clax-do-vfs's 16 MiB transaction cap (vfs/src/lib.rs MAX_TRANSACTION_BYTES) with room for rows and indexes: a version or push carrying more is refused, invalid_argument, with the bound in the message (git shows it after 'remote:' or as HTTP 413). Each object is one row, whole, so a single file over the bound can never be stored. Artifacts allows 32 MB per blob and 1 GB per repository. delete (db.rs:117) runs DELETE FROM git_objects WHERE id NOT IN (SELECT id FROM git_held), a scan of every object, on each repository deletion.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"6183d1a70eeca3ee16eaaf4607a156c177d6eb02f1ae847cba00067497ce28a4"},"summary":"The stand-in takes at most 12 MiB of objects in one push or publish, and drops unheld objects with a full scan on every repository deletion","supersedes":"5aaa4d81eeb6f3d689fa1dac9f27328090191b0eca61c8990121ea5ec1f4abd2","tags":["limits","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"59d38ab19394eb4285cc02b671efa9d84a25eb7a264db2a9d5f632f4844db5b4","body":{"detail":"tokens::mint asks the host for the token, then its remote, then writes the ledger row. On Cloudflare Artifacts createToken has made a live token by then; if remote() (a get and info()) or insert_token fails, mint answers the error and the token is neither returned nor in git_tokens, so nothing can revoke it before its TTL (at most what the caller asked, PERSON_TOKEN_TTL_S or AGENT_TOKEN_TTL_S). Ask for the remote first, or enter the row in the must-revoke list when the insert fails.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":238},"end":{"line":248},"content_hash":"b8ece7fef497593a251599cd340472d0c2db6aa91ef14618db26be51da22c4c7"},"summary":"A token the host minted is live but untracked when remote() or the ledger insert fails after it","supersedes":"8e60c81a2218e10787dc9044745317712e2afd4563c40833b4194b0b5e16f92e","tags":["security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:20.462173Z","id":"ad7c6df82190e149fec6b6cb35510a0190fdc88abbf6e648aa3acfb5152435fa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:608a2267","summary":"Fixed in 608a2267: RepoDO builds its parts at the first event (Built::new); a failure answers 503 with the reason, is logged and is tried again at the next event; no expect remains in RepoDO::new. Evidence: (cd crates/clax-worker && cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings) clean, cargo test 70 passed, node test-wasm.mjs ok. No test makes the build fail (the stand-in's storage cannot be made to fail under wrangler dev).","supersedes":"a8df47c875e190a12525e8ac933ca54d40d72d61783ec6e960121f25f0b7e45e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:20.470814Z","id":"fda800ae8a1af373d00009e89b916242e9b7857fcf1af47e0b801e20682979cd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:608a2267","summary":"Fixed in 608a2267: Built::new takes repo_store(env)?, so an unknown REPO_STORE fails RepoDO's build (503 'Unknown REPO_STORE', every event) as content_store does, instead of falling back to the stand-in.","supersedes":"ca3c96c535ecb30457946bf97b16485f3532260c2fc452702f650022ae197e87","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
